2026-09-27 B08b: standard excess precision uses existing source-format semantics.

Authority: EvoIR 1.9.112 section 3.13, FLT_EVAL_METHOD=0.
GCC 14.2's option description requires casts and assignments to round to their
semantic types; it does not require an excess-precision carrier where none is
used. https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc-14.2.0/gcc/Optimize-Options.html#index-fexcess-precision
EvoCC already rounds each source operation as well as casts/assignments; this
patch admits the explicit option without changing that numerical contract.
It does not enable fast/16 modes, dynamic rounding, contraction or Annex F.

Source SHA256 f83f0507f5eaf5e91b4e63ae4ad2ed04561df3d76c026113f41b50995c961fe1.
Tested debug compiler SHA256
5e5a5816af87ad0a53652fffe87ffe27d9f073ad412b8f0ba1ae4b6db15c3e3a.
The benchmark frozen 523a6982 subject remains unchanged and does not inherit
this later driver change. Numerical implementation is unchanged.

RED: frozen driver rejects -fexcess-precision=standard before source execution.
The projection RED fails its exact ordered-argv assertion because the option
is dropped. GREEN retains the option in E0 and both mixed/subject projectors.

The C case checks source-format cancellation for binary32/64/128, assignment
and explicit narrowing casts, and the direct decimal-to-binary32 discriminator.
GCC14/Clang19 O0/O2 with fixed/dynamic flags: eight sealed AArch64 native PASS.
Actual EvoCC assembly at O0/O2 with both flags, assembled/linked by both fixed
reference compilers: eight native PASS. Both interpreters return zero.
For preprocess, both interpreters, canonical IR and assembly, each O0/O2 and
fixed/dynamic combination is byte-identical with zero, one or two copies of
the standard-precision option. Fast, 16, unknown and fast-math combinations
remain explicit refusals. 527 CLI tests, Clippy and fmt pass; 262 ladder tests
and Ruff pass. No second numerical path or metadata field is introduced.

The same eight original musl commands are replayed with the new option:
__math_oflow, __math_uflow, frexp and scalbn emit; ARM64 ceil/floor/rint/rintf
still reject scalar FP w-constrained assembly with E3021. For every command,
exit, stdout and stderr are identical with/without the option. The remaining
listed omissions and scalar-assembly boundary are not waived. This closes
one command-projection subcase, not B08, libc-test or faithful full musl build.

Raw logs: .build/floating-targeted/strict-20260927/excess-*.log.
